# Rahfi's Portfolio (frontend): environment reference
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the real value by hand. `.env` is gitignored and is
# never read, printed, or copied by anyone, including an AI assistant, per
# docs/rules/env.rules.md. Only this example file is ever opened.
#
# Keep this file in step with the code: a new variable is added here in the same
# commit that introduces it, so the example never falls behind what runs.
#
# NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ PREFIX
# Nothing in this file carries the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and nothing may be given
# it. A prefixed value is compiled into the JavaScript bundle the browser
# downloads and is public the moment it ships. The one value the browser needs,
# the backend's address, is written on the page's <html> element instead. See
# docs/rules/secret.rules.md.
#
# WHY THERE IS ONLY ONE VARIABLE
# The browser calls the backend directly, and the pages read published content
# from it, so this site holds no secret at all. Every variable it used to hold
# moved to the backend's environment, on the backend-main and backend-dev
# branches, or was removed:
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  the backend reads published content and
#                                    keeps the visitor counters with them
#   GITHUB_TOKEN                     the backend serves the GitHub statistics
#   RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY               the backend hands it to the contact page,
#                                    beside the secret it pairs with
#   STUDIO_SERVICE_KEY               removed: nothing forwards a visitor's
#                                    address any more, so nothing vouches for it
# The model key, the mail password, and the storage service account are not
# environment variables at all; they are set in /studio > Settings.


# The backend
# Its origin, with no path. Not a secret. Read when the site is built as well as
# when it runs, so set it before the first production build. Locally it defaults
# to http://localhost:8000 when unset. Always localhost, never 127.0.0.1: the two
# are different sites to a browser, and the studio's cookie would not be sent.
BACKEND_URL=https://api.rahfi.pro
